You have an Azure subscription.

You create an Azure Resource Manager (ARM) template file named deploy.json. The template defines

a StorageV2 storage account that uses a Premium_LRS SKU. The resource name is generated

dynamically by combining an index value with a unique string, and the template uses a copy loop to

deploy multiple instances of the storage account.

{

"$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/

deploymentTemplate.json#",

"contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",

"parameters": {

"location": {

"type": "string",

"defaultValue": "westus"

}

},

"resources": [

{

"apiVersion": "2019-04-01",

"type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",

"name": "[concat(copyIndex(), 'storage', uniqueString(resourceGroup().id))]",

"location": "[resourceGroup().location]",

"sku": {

"name": "Premium_LRS"

},

"kind": "StorageV2",

"properties": {},

"copy": {

"name": "storagecopy",

"count": 3

}

}

]

}

You then connect to the subscription and run the following commands.

New-AZResourceGroup -Name RG1 -Location "centralus"

New-AZResourceGroupDeployment -ResourceGroupName RG1 -TemplateFile

"deploy.json"

